cs42l84: use the kernel's name for the jack preamp control

The cs42l84 driver as merged in Linux (and in Asahi's tree) names the
control "ADC Preamp Capture Volume", so macaudio exposes it as
"Jack ADC Preamp Capture Volume". The Headset EnableSequence still set
"Jack ADC Preamp Gain", which fails, so enabling the Headset device fails
and the headset microphone is never routed.

--- a/ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/cs42l84/Headphones.conf
+++ b/ucm2/conf.d/macaudio/cs42l84/Headphones.conf
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
 		cset "name='Jack WNF Corner Frequency' 1"
 		cset "name='Jack ADC HPF Switch' on"
 		cset "name='Jack HPF Corner Frequency' 1"
-		cset "name='Jack ADC Preamp Gain' 2"
+		cset "name='Jack ADC Preamp Capture Volume' 2"
 		cset "name='Jack SDOUT1 Select' 'ADC'"
 	]
 
